# Fabric delete cascade

Follow the standard Fabric pattern:

**Deleting upstream destroys downstream. Deleting downstream leaves upstream intact.**

Examples (report ↔ semantic model):

- Delete a **report** → the bound **semantic model remains** (may leave an orphan model).
- Delete a **semantic model** → the **service** removes dependent reports (and related tiles). The CLI does not control or defeat that cascade.

## Confirmations

Unless `-s` / `--silent`, delete and overwrite confirms must **name every known affected object** (type, display name, id) — not only counts.

- Upstream delete: list the model **and** each discovered downstream report before proceeding.
- Downstream delete: list the report; note the upstream model left behind when known.
- Shared-model overwrite: list other consumers that will be affected.

## Do not

- Invent CLI flags that pretend to leave dangling reports after a model delete (the service cascades).
- Cascade-delete a model when the user only deleted a report.
